tender_description:
Highways England is seeking the provision of services to undertake research into weaving lengths, junction spacing and datum points. Specifically, this project will look at:
1)	The suitability of current requirements for weaving lengths on motorway and all-purpose trunk roads for both urban and rural situations; 
2)	The scope of 'reserved lanes' in relation to weaving;
3)	Minimum spacing requirements for dual carriageway to single carriageway transitions at lane drop/lane gain arrangements, as illustrated in Figure 1 below; 
4)	The suitability of the current requirement for the minimum spacing of priority junctions from the end of dual carriageway/single carriageway transitions; and
5)	Datum points for All-Purpose Trunk Roads (APTR).

Newcastle City Council (NCC) and Your Homes Newcastle (YHN) are seeking to appoint partners to provide water hygiene services to NCC public buildings and YHN properties in accordance with 'The Control of Legionella Bacteria in Water Systems' L8 Approved Code of Practice 2013 and HSG274 Parts 2&3: The control of legionella bacteria in hot and cold water systems and other systems or the latest legislation and regulations set down in law for the duration of this framework contract.

The Contract period is for 24 months subject to performance with a further 2 x 12 month options to extend, again subject to performance.  

