Project description: provision of air quality monitoring services, including the provision of electronic publically available information, for the four automatic monitoring stations in the borough as outlined below. The service delivery must be in accordance with the Defra LAQM TG16 guidance, London LAQM TG16 guidance and the procedures as outlined in the AURN manual for the national air quality monitoring network. The data must be made publicly available and the Council provided with

Date required - delivery date/works to commence on: 1st November 2018

The project
The London Borough of Hillingdon wishes to secure the continuation of the provision of air quality monitoring at the council-supported monitoring stations in the borough. The provision is being sought for one year. The Council will consider the optional supplement of a quote for additional years of provision, any discount for extended years should be made clear.

The council supported stations are:
-	Hillingdon South Ruislip (NO2 and PM10) - the air quality monitoring station and analysers are owned by the Council, the site is managed by an external contractor;
-	Hillingdon Sipson (NO2) - this is provided and managed by an external contractor;
-	Hillingdon Hayes (NO2 and PM10) - this is provided and managed by an external contractor;
-	Hillingdon Oxford Avenue (NO2 and PM10) - this is provided and managed by an external contractor;

