The Client (UKAEA) seeks to create a better understanding of the high tensile deformation behaviour of Eurofer97 steel under a 0.5T permanent magnetic field at elevated temperatures (550 Â°C).

UKAEA wishes to appoint a Consultant to provide tensile testing of Eurofer97 both with and without the application of a 0.5T magnetic field at 550 Â°C.  The EU DEMO and possibly STEP reactors will impose a high magnetic field on the blanket structural materials, of which Eurofer97 is a potential candidate.  Any degradation to the engineering properties under a magnetic field will affect the engineering design allowable used for Eurofer97 in future fusion reactors design. Hence, it is important to understand the effect of applied magnetic fields on high temperature tensile properties for Eurofer97 steel during the conceptual design phase, so any effects can be considered during down selection of component designs.

UKAEA wishes to appoint a Consultant that can fulfil three essential criteria including:
Experience of performing experiments under a magnetic field

Excellent research track records on the understanding of the deformation mechanisms of alloys;

Has equipment that can meet our specifications and only requiring a small amount of equipment development;

â¢	Security Testing and Vulnerability Analysis - such as Penetration testing, the provision of suitably (Check or Crest) qualified individuals able to perform application and infrastructure security testing in line with CESG requirements; 
â¢	Security Assessment and audits â the provision of CLAS/ISO27001 Lead Auditors, who can perform all tests/audits against government standards/ISO27001/good practice;
â¢	Security consultancy â the provision of suitably (Check or Crest) qualified individuals to deliver specific security-related advice and consultancy in the areas of, but not limited to technology, architecture, risk assessment, risk treatment (as part of the ISO27001 ISMS risk assessment report) and threat assessment;
â¢	Security assurance â the provision of suitably (Check or Crest) qualified individuals to carry out assurance activities, including but not limited to supplier compliance reviews;
â¢	Forensics and investigations â the provision of suitably (Check or Crest) qualified individuals to conduct forensic and investigatory work, including but not limited to on site forensics, general security investigations and disk analysis.

